ORDINANCE XIII OF 1970
ORDINANCE XIII OF 1970
NATIONAL AND PROVINCIAL
ASSEMBLIES (ELECTIONS) ORDINANCE, 1970
CHAPTER I‑PRELIMINARY
2. Definitions.‑In
this Ordinance, unless there is anything repugnant in~ the subject or
context,‑
(f) "Assembly" means the National Assembly
of Pakistan or a Provincial: Assembly for a province provided for in the Legal
Framework Order,_ 1970 ;
(ii) "ballot paper account" means a ballot
paper account prepared under subsection (10) of section 36 ;
(iii) "candidate" means a person proposed
as a candidate for election as a member ;
(iv) "Commission" means the Election
Commission constituted under the Legal Framework Order, 1970 ;
(v) "Commissioner" means the Chief Election
Commissioner appointed or deemed to be appointed under the Electoral Rolls
Order, 1969 ;
(vi) "constituency"
means a constituency delimited under the Delimitation of Constituencies Order,
1970, for the purpose of election of a member ;
(vii) "contesting candidate" means a
candidate who has been validly nominated for election as a member and has not
withdrawn his candidature ;
(viii) "election" means election to a seat
of a member held under this Ordinance ;
(ix) "election agent" means an election
agent appointed by a candidate under section 21 and, where no such appointment is
made, the candidate acting as his own election agent ;
(x) "election petition" means an election
petition made under section 50 ;
(ii) "elector", in relation to a
constituency, means a person who is enrolled on the electoral roll for any
electoral area in that constituency ;
(xii) "electoral roll" means an electoral
roll prepared under the Electoral Rolls Order, 1969 ;
(xiii) "member" means
a member of an Assembly ;
(xiv) "nomination day" means the day
appointed under section 11 for the nomination of candidates ;
(xv) "polling agent" means a polling agent
appointed under section 22 ;
(xvi) "polling day" means the day on which
poll is taken for an election ;
(xvii) "polling officer" means a polling
officer appointed under section 9 for a polling station ;
(xviii) "prescribed" means prescribed by
rules made under this Ordinance ;
(xix) "Presiding Officer" means a Presiding
Officer appointed under section 9 for a polling station and includes an
Assistant Presiding Officer exercising the powers and performing the functions
of Presiding Officer ;
(xx) "returned candidate" means a candidate
who has been declared .elected as a member under this Ordinance ;
(xxi) "Returning Officer" means a Returning
Officer appointed under section 7 and includes an Assistant Returning Officer
exercising the powers and performing the functions of Returning Officer ;
(xxii) "scrutiny day" means the day
appointed under section 11 for the scrutiny of nomination papers ;
(xxiii) "spoilt ballot paper" means a
ballot paper which has been spoiled :and is returned to the Presiding Officer
under section 34 ;
(xxiv) "Tribunal" means an Election
Tribunal appointed under section 54 for the trial of election petitions ;
(xxv) "withdrawal day" means the day
appointed under section I1 on .or before which candidature may be withdrawn.
